-- title:
--   Galois representation on the Taylor–Wiles Hecke module, strict ordinary case
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over $k$ (a rank-two $k$-module with a $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$-action trivial on some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$) which is absolutely irreducible. Let $S\supseteq S_{\min}\ni p$ be finite sets of primes such that for a prime $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $(X-1)^2$ for every $\sigma$ in inertia at a place above $q$. Let $N\neq0$ be squarefree, with all prime divisors in $S$, divisible by every $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$, with every prime divisor $\neq p$ lying in $S_{\min}$, and with $p\mid N$; assume $\bar\rho$, viewed as an adic representation over $k$, is not finite flat at $p$ in the sense of `GaloisRep.IsFlatAt`. Let $r\geq5$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, and $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at every place above $r$. Assume the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by those with integral $q$-expansion coefficients, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) such that $\det(X-\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes outside $S$ with $p\mid q_i-1$, and $\alpha_i\in k$ with $\alpha_i^2-\theta(T_{q_i})\alpha_i+q_i=0$ and $2\alpha_i\neq\theta(T_{q_i})$. Let $\mathrm{cyc}_q$ be homomorphisms from the Galois group to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ which for $q$ prime give the mod-$q$ cyclotomic character ($\sigma\mu=\mu^{\mathrm{cyc}_q(\sigma)}$ for $\mu^q=1$), and $\pi_{\Delta,q}\colon(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\to \mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q-1)}$ homomorphisms, surjective for primes $q\neq p$. Put $L=N\prod_i q_i\cdot r$, let $H_R\leq(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$ and $H_Q=H_R\cap\ker\pi_Q$, where $\pi_Q$ is the product of the $\pi_{\Delta,q_i}$ composed with reduction; assume the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$) and $U_{q_i}$ on $H^1(L,H_Q;\mathcal O)$ commute pairwise, and that the diamond operators commute with them. Write $M_Q$ for the localisation of $H^1(L,H_Q;\mathcal O)$ at the complement of the kernel of the map $\mathcal O[X_g]\to k$ sending $T_\ell\mapsto\theta(T_\ell)$ and $U_{q_i}\mapsto\alpha_i$. Then there exists a complete local Noetherian commutative ring $\mathbb T$, finite as an $\mathcal O$-module via a local $\mathcal O$-algebra structure, with $\mathcal O\to\mathbb T/\mathfrak m_{\mathbb T}$ surjective, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{act}\colon\mathbb T\to\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(M_Q)$, a homomorphism $\mathrm{dia}\colon\prod_i\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}\to\mathbb T^\times$, automorphisms $\kappa_i$ of $\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$, and a rank-two adically continuous Galois representation $\rho$ over $\mathbb T$ such that: $\rho$ has cyclotomic determinant, is strictly ordinary at $p$, is unramified outside $S_{\min}\cup\{q_1,\dots,q_t\}$, and has $(X-1)^2$ as inertial characteristic polynomial at each prime $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$; the residual representation of $\rho$ is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along $k\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathbb T$; for $u\in H_R$, $\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{dia}(\pi_Q(u)))$ is the diamond operator of $u$ on $M_Q$; for each prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and each Frobenius $\sigma$ at a place above $\ell$, there is $u\in H_R$ with $\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma))$ acting on $M_Q$ as $T_\ell$ followed by the diamond operator of $u$; and for each $i$ and each place above $q_i$ there is a $\mathbb T$-basis $b_0,b_1$ of $\rho$ on which inertia at $q_i$ acts by $\mathrm{dia}$ of the $i$-th component $\kappa_i(\pi_{\Delta,q_i}(\mathrm{cyc}_{q_i}(\sigma)))$ on $b_0$ and by its inverse on $b_1$.
--
--   This is the Taylor–Wiles-level analogue of the construction of the Galois representation attached to a localised Hecke module, in the case $p\mid N$ where the residual representation is not finite flat at $p$, so that the representation produced satisfies the strict ordinarity condition at $p$ and is ramified at the auxiliary Taylor–Wiles primes $q_i$ through a diagonal character valued in $\Delta_Q$. It is the input to the comparison with the universal deformation ring, [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_deformationRing_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_deformationRing_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary).
